  "notes": [
    "A WebSocket connection opens with an HTTP GET handshake, so the client's connect is an http link to the endpoint path (contract GET /path); its server is the addEndpoint(...) line of registerStompEndpoints, with the method's declaration as an alternative.",
    "STOMP frames are messaging links, producer to consumer. A client SEND to /app/x (the application destination prefix from setApplicationDestinationPrefixes) is consumed by @MessageMapping(\"/x\"); a reply via @SendTo(\"/topic/y\") is produced by the annotated method and consumed by the client's subscribe('/topic/y'). Destinations are written in full, prefix included.",
    "The client is ng2-stomp-service's StompService, configured with stomp.configure({host: '/stomp-websocket'}) (a relative SockJS URL); send and subscribe are methods of the same injected service."
  ]
